Dump keyword-filtered strings from logd's tracev3 files to the console
(sweetlogdump).

No userland probe can become a process on this port (v25 custom launchd job
never execs; v26 probe as /usr/libexec/driverkitd leaves no EXECW), so read the
logs from the kernel instead: enumerate the tracev3 files of
/private/var/db/diagnostics/Persist, read them in 8 KiB chunks and print the
printable strings that match the same keyword list the userland logdump used.

Off unless sweetlogdump=1; all paths/times/limits are boot-arg controlled:

  sweetlogdump=1                    enable
  sweetlogtimes=240,420[,600]       boot uptimes to dump at (default 240,420)
  sweetlogmax=300                   max matched lines per dump (default 300)
  sweetlogdir=<dir>                 default /private/var/db/diagnostics/Persist
                                    (can point at .../Special or .../Signpost)

Per dump:
  KLOG --- dump <n> at <uptime> s: <nfiles> tracev3 files
  KLOG file <name> size=<n>
  KLOG| <matched printable string>     (<=200 chars, non-printables dropped)
  KLOG end <lines> lines

Implementation notes: directory entries are parsed with the kernel's own
`struct dirent` (32-bit ino layout; KERNEL builds define
__DARWIN_64_BIT_INO_T=0), which is what VNOP_READDIR(flags=0) returns on HFS
(STD_DIRENT_LEN packing).  Captured strings come from printable runs >= 6
chars inside the raw file; tracev3 payload chunks are LZ4-compressed, so this
patch sees the uncompressed metadata/header strings - if that turns out too
thin, a follow-up can add a bounded LZ4 block decoder.

Base: bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c after 0126 and 0128; only that file changes.
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c
